	(text "QUAD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.75 65.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0583a89b-3944-4f3b-a0f1-0aa53e886357")
	)
	(text "F6 / F7: 200 mA PTC (TECHFUSE SMD0603-020-24V, 0.55 ohm) in series with the 5 V\noption only (JP1 / JP4 1-2). RC_5V is the RoboClaw BEC, which also feeds the\nRoboClaw logic: a shorted or miswired encoder cable on the 5 V setting would\ndrag it down. F6/F7 trip at 500 mA and reset when the fault clears. Hold current\ncovers an E6B2-CWZ6C (80 mA) with margin; drop at 80 mA is about 50 mV. The 3.3 V\noption has F3 (100 mA), the 12 V option F4 (350 mA). The 1k pull-ups stay on\nRC_5V unfused (20 mA worst case)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150 192 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10ee99a3-fd75-4578-93a2-419d3bfafb1f")
	)
	(text "2V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.76 95.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "13314fb5-e38c-42c0-b860-b14cdf0929c6")
	)
	(text "The encoder connectors J8/J9 (field-wired) take their 3.3 V option from U18 (TPS70933, 30 V max,\nfrom RC_5V), not 3V3_CM4, so a miswired sensor supply cannot back-feed the CM4 or the GPS. U18 \nblocks reverse current, so it cannot reach RC_5V either. EN: R110 100k pull-up to RC_5V, TP37\nfor test (ground TP37 to hold U18 off). Never tie EN straight to IN.\nF3 (100 mA PTC) sits between J9 and D23 (SMBJ3V3); F3 limits a shorted cable or a miswire\nonto J8/J9 while D23 clamps U18 OUT (7 V abs max). C81 >= 1.5 uF effective."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.538 164.084 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1435ea78-55ce-42d6-ab14-d593e0a3135d")
	)
	(text "QUAD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
