		(uuid "83f06ada-379f-4af0-841d-08b4930360c8")
	)
	(text "JUMPERS  (ENC1: JP1 JP2 JP3, ENC2: JP4 JP5 JP6)\nJP1/JP4  V+ supply   1-2: 5 V (RC_5V via F6/F7, 200 mA PTC)\n                     3-4: 3.3 V (ENC_3V3, U18)\n                     5-6: 12 V (ENC_12V, battery)\n         Shunt across a row only: 1-3 or 3-5 shorts two rails.\nJP2/JP5  mode        1-3 + 2-4: QUAD\n                     3-5 + 4-6: ABS\nJP3/JP6  ABS scale   1-2: 3.3 V sensor -> 2 V\n                     2-3: 0-2 V direct\nDefault ENC1 (Firgelli): 5V, QUAD\nDefault ENC2 (AS5600): 3.3V, ABS, 3V3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 207.01 156.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8a6575c6-cf13-4a22-98fd-1d6d045026ca")
	)
	(text "LIMIT SWITCHES: the RoboClaw has one limit input per motor (S4 = M1, S5 = M2) and supports two\nswitches on it. Wire two NC switches in SERIES per axis (J12 elevation, J13 azimuth): either one\nopening lets the 4.7k pull-up raise the input. Set Invert (active-high). Both switches share the\npin, so the RoboClaw takes fwd/rev from the commanded direction: set S4/S5 to Limit(Both), or to\nHome(User)/Limit(Fwd) with the retract-end switch on the reverse side so it also zeroes the\nencoder (elevation, Firgelli). NO switches would go in parallel instead. J12/J13 are 2-pin:\ndaisy-chain the second switch in the field wiring.\nThe E-stop and limit loops run at 12 V (ENC_12V): R48/R52/R55 4.7k pull-ups pass about 2.6 mA through the closed contacts\n(contact wetting on long cable runs); open, the node sits at battery voltage (10-14.6 V) and the 47k/20k\ndivider (R50/R109, R54/R107, R56/R108) delivers 3.0-4.4 V to S3/S4/S5 (5 V tolerant); C58/C60/C61 10 nF, tau 0.14 ms.\nD17/D19/D20 are 15 V ESD parts for the 12 V nodes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 238.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8f405950-873e-40c0-a4e1-6895e9573a28")
	)
	(text "U18 EN (pin 3): R110 100k pull-up to RC_5V, TP37 for test. Ground TP37 to hold U18 off,\nrelease to run. EN clamps at 6.5 V: keep TP37 under 6 V and never tie EN straight to IN."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.538 176.022 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9cdaf491-e452-4588-8f38-5657a54e15f3")
	)
	(text "EMC: run motor leads in shielded cable, shield\nclamped 360 deg to the enclosure at the gland\n(not to J11/J14). Clip-on CM ferrite per pair at\nentry; 100 nF brush caps at the motors. Keep\nmotor leads away from GNSS/encoder wiring."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.088 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9e250d5e-0632-4b07-b02f-ea2918db1f2e")
	)
	(text "J11 = Firgelli motor (elevation):\n1 BLUE  (+)\n2 BROWN (-)\nSwap to reverse, or\ninvert M1 in Motion Studio."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 73.66 172.212 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a361fa3d-1da6-4189-884d-7e1b4cfbdd92")
	)
	(text "ABS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b239fe31-f433-4568-a585-b878091266cf")
	)
	(text "E-stop and limits: 12 V loops, NC,\nset Invert. 2 limits/motor: see note."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 294.64 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d1396d18-68e0-4e85-95a9-f6bc3b4f18a1")
	)
	(text "Motors Output\nM1 = elevation\nM2 = azimuth"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 68.834 147.828 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e21c84d4-91d3-48ad-b284-786741b02ccd")
	)
	(text "RC_5V budget: <= 800 mA (BEC).\nLoad: ~20 mA pull-ups + sensors.\nF6/F7: 200 mA PTC, 5 V option."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 72.39 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f2de7e5d-e19d-4e62-b25e-754e81c7ca60")
	)
	(text "Battery voltage (10-14.6 V) for sensors that need it (E6B2-CWZ6C: 5-24 V, 80 mA)\nand the E-stop / limit-switch loops (4.7k pull-ups). From V_MOTOR, so the return stays on\nthe RoboClaw ground. F4 350 mA PTC, D28 SMAJ20A, C89 10 uF. Encoder pull-ups: RC_5V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.28 184.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f4545f8c-c492-4a45-830b-4766ba7df511")
	)
	(text "A1 RX buffer (no CM4 back-power)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 289.052 171.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "fac9be80-b006-4897-adf1-21d5092f4ece")
	)
	(text "ROBOCLAW-2X15A-OEM"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
